The endpoints (-3,4) and (4,-3) lie on the circle and are excluded.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1957_AMC_12_Q34","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_202","cnm_146","cnm_150"],"id":"substitute-and-factor","label":"Substitute and factor","methodDirectNodeIds":{"substitute-and-factor":["cnm_094","cnm_h024"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_094","cnm_h024","cnm_202","cnm_146","cnm_150"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7767d43cedf134eacc7f780f"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, x-y+z+1","reason":"Writing w = y-z gives x^2-w^2+x+w = (x+w)(x-w+1). Thus the original expression is (x+y-z)(x-y+z+1).","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1963_AMC_12_Q21","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"id":"recognize-and-group","label":"Recognize a square and factor","methodDirectNodeIds":{"recognize-and-group":["cnm_154","cnm_153","cnm_152","cnm_151"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_154","cnm_153","cnm_152","cnm_151","cnm_150"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7767d43cedf134eacc7f780f"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 20<P<30","reason":"(x-2)(x-3)<0 gives 2<x<3. On this interval P=(x+2)(x+3) is strictly increasing, with endpoint values 20 and 30, neither attained.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1967_AMC_12_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_150","cnm_096"],"id":"solution:positive-factor-bounds:474d3e65bc02","label":"Factor and bound positive factors","methodDirectNodeIds":{"positive-factor-bounds":["cnm_h024","cnm_h029","cnm_h018"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h024","cnm_h029","cnm_h018","cnm_150","cnm_096"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7767d43cedf134eacc7f780f"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: -1","reason":"Because n is a root, n^2+mn+n=n(n+m+1)=0. Since n is nonzero, m+n=-1. The pair m=1, n=-2 confirms consistency.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1968_AMC_12_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_029","cnm_040","cnm_150"],"id":"substitute-root","label":"Use the meaning of a root","methodDirectNodeIds":{"substitute-root":["cnm_039","cnm_151"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_039","cnm_151","cnm_029","cnm_040","cnm_150"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7767d43cedf134eacc7f780f"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 9","reason":"The factorization is (x-k)(x+k+1), so n = k(k+1). The values k = 1 through 9 work because 9 × 10 ≤ 100 < 10 × 11, giving nine values.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1989_AMC_12_Q08","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_146","cnm_150","cnm_014"],"id":"match-integer-factor-coefficients","label":"Determine the possible integer factors","methodDirectNodeIds":{"match-integer-factor-coefficients":["math:integer-diophantine-equations","math:factorization-coefficient-comparison"]},"nodeIds":["math:integer-diophantine-equations","math:factorization-coefficient-comparison","cnm_146","cnm_150","cnm_014"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7767d43cedf134eacc7f780f"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B. One positive integer","reason":"The expression factors as (n-1)(n-2). It is zero for n=1,2, equals the prime 2 for n=3, and is a product of two integers greater than 1 for every n>=4. Thus only n=3 works.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2002_AMC_10B_Q06","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_150","cnm_p153"],"id":"factor-and-classify","label":"Expose the factors","methodDirectNodeIds":{"factor-and-classify":["cnm_151","cnm_155","cnm_p157"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_151","cnm_155","cnm_p157","cnm_150","cnm_p153"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7767d43cedf134eacc7f780f"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A. 7/2","reason":"Factoring gives (2x+3)(2x-10)=0. The roots are -3/2 and 5, whose sum is 7/2. Expansion also gives 4x^2-14x-30=0, with root sum 14/4.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2002_AMC_12A_Q01","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_150","cnm_042","cnm_010"],"id":"solution:factor-and-add-roots:c43899f53194","label":"Use the shared factor","methodDirectNodeIds":{"factor-and-add-roots":["cnm_151","cnm_224"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_151","cnm_224","cnm_150","cnm_042","cnm_010"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7767d43cedf134eacc7f780f"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 16.5","reason":"Factoring gives (x - b)(2x - a - c) = 0, so the root sum is (a + b + c + b)/2. Distinct digits satisfy a + b + c <= 24 and b <= 9, giving a bound of 33/2, attained by (a, b, c) = (8, 9, 7).","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_150"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2015_AMC_10B_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_150","cnm_042"],"id":"factor-and-bound","label":"Expose the roots and prove an attainable bound","methodDirectNodeIds":{"factor-and-bound":["cnm_151","cnm_224","math:extremal-principle"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_151","cnm_224","math:extremal-principle","cnm_150","cnm_042"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:7767d43cedf134eacc7f780f"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, x = 26","reason":"Adding